    {
      "id": "03-fats",
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "fats",
      "text": "5 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 13 milligrams, so the cholesterol row stays controlled. Saturated fat is 2.4 grams, a moderate tradeoff rather than a huge problem. Polyunsaturated fat is only 0.2 grams, so this is not where the useful fats come from. For dairy, fat quality can help, but it can also drag the entry down.",
      "textSha256": "7c0e0ef99699981bc8751d9d6787fc36feb837acf3dcd8a6a28ec4e498c7d26f",
      "characterCount": 319,
      "byteLength": 385402,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "7UQwGxGgEV5DsmGanck7",
        "historyItemId": "YS32E2wRAr7CNNxOJoyM"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "4 grams of carbs. Glycemic index is 11, so the carb behaviour is very steady. Sugar is 4 grams, which stays fairly controlled for plain dairy. Fibre is 0 grams, so there is no fibre-based fullness here. For dairy, carbs mostly come down to sugar control.",
      "textSha256": "c82a1a2565d98b4aec3264aad1bfef306d59263886f84fe9d19d3fdbd2424d91",
      "characterCount": 254,
      "byteLength": 294705,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "FQ8GPGF67hdOA8tpa3vz",
        "historyItemId": "xTYKMRgzZbPPTiqMocpj"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "9 grams of protein. That clears the useful-protein gate, but the amount is still moderate rather than huge. Essential amino acids score is 7 out of 9, and bioavailability is 90%, so the quality side is much stronger than the amount. For dairy, useful protein is one of the main reasons it works.",
      "textSha256": "a6df88912ec116464a810d2eaa1ea6f2527d3152d3c976419bf6b85877b99364",
      "characterCount": 295,
      "byteLength": 328142,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "jTMQtk2P2IrQVSsplKEZ",
        "historyItemId": "Yyf1KSpAGbrg8Yyd1qiu"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamin B12 is 31% daily value, the clear vitamin strength. Vitamin A is only 2% daily value, so there is not much backup vitamin support. For dairy, B12 helps a lot, but this is not a broad vitamin win.",
      "textSha256": "9002734a4badf3ccb032e6add5e81f72f0e1ba0d068e09923c8b703362d689ba",
      "characterCount": 203,
      "byteLength": 258760,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "Rk42niXQiwzAwdmqIqWu",
        "historyItemId": "w2OLIPfxrxMt6Xy71VVf"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Calcium is 8% daily value, the best mineral number but still too low to carry the section. Zinc is 5% daily value, and magnesium is 3% daily value, so the backup minerals are light too. For dairy, calcium is the obvious mineral check, and here it is not high enough.",
      "textSha256": "6d048bdd8ff71e24d6b7432ba3f73bfceaff0b483ef9ce138471de6bda6ab14f",
      "characterCount": 266,
      "byteLength": 297631,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "lrcJNdaDB4AbNFEzeb1S",
        "historyItemId": "u3H0kNQotLIUUWbmT8a9"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Pros first: fermented-food angle adds extra value. Plain Greek yogurt can bring live-culture context that plain milk does not. Thick texture helps satiety. The strained texture makes it more filling than many softer dairy options. Helps make meals feel complete. It works as a simple base for breakfasts, bowls, sauces, or snacks.",
      "textSha256": "ed7cd4f3c65f4ec26318b1879b58f301c91d6d765b8dc50ed2b5dc3914741a97",
      "characterCount": 330,
      "byteLength": 327306,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "ZCNkodP5PF3r1gE0GAxu",
        "historyItemId": "clW4Q2G0C97qpb9lfivf"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: dairy tolerance can be a barrier. Lactose sensitivity or dairy avoidance can make it a poor fit for some people. Sweetened versions change the profile fast. The plain record is strong, but common flavoured tubs can add a lot of sugar. Format choices can drag it down fast. The exact tub and how it is used matter a lot.",
      "textSha256": "adcbbc478adde1064328c40cea9b18fd01b4a297319863f744ca472e27e26f1e",
      "characterCount": 330,
      "byteLength": 351965,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "3o3m9R8aYTBid6gtOzAl",
        "historyItemId": "CEa6st2LcQuAK6mNicOP"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are steady carbs, vitamin B12, useful protein quality, and practical meal fit. Weak spots are light minerals, low vitamin A, and no fibre. Best for practical meals, satiety, and simple protein support because it is thick, steady, and easy to use without adding sugar.",
      "textSha256": "bab49a5fe24817559aa590b5245bd720267944f534e090fb2a3652725ac8e3ac",
      "characterCount": 277,
      "byteLength": 335247,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice-v1-blocks/10-closing_summary.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "0WBwvBAm1LrEb9QC6Z5s",
        "historyItemId": "XK0qywI4ALdFYPn1xU0E"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/greek-yogurt/voice/voice-v1-blocks/10-closing_summary.mp3"
    },
